{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And they were opened, etc.</b> Regarding knowledge the verse speaks, not regarding actual sight — and the end of the verse proves it." "<b>And they knew that they were naked.</b> Even a blind person knows when he is naked. So what is וַיֵּדְעוּ כִּי עֵירֻמִּם הֵם? One commandment was in their hand, and they were stripped of it (Bereshit Rabbah)." "<b>Fig tree.</b> This is the tree they ate from — by the very thing through which they ruined themselves they were repaired (Sanhedrin 70). But the rest of the trees prevented them from taking their leaves. And why was the tree not publicized? Because the Holy One, blessed be He, does not wish to mortify a creature, so that people will not shame it and say: This is the one through which the world was struck — Midrash of Rabbi Tanchuma."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:22.864903331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}